## Cycle 2 — 2026-08-03 — fresh reviewer, no cycle-1 memory — VERDICT: findings

Hard rules passed again, including a whole-package portability sweep. Five new Criticals, all
fixed in this round:

- **C2-1 The canonical-identifier rule did not fit three of four always-on angles.** Mandating a
  `<DATABASE>-<ENTRY>` id forces an agent surveying control standards, incident records or
  conference talks to either invent a registry-shaped id or drop real candidates. FIXED: an
  identifier policy per source class, with an explicit non-registry form (stable URL + published
  title + retrieval date) for disclosure-class items, and C15 now grades the policy rather than
  one pattern.
- **C2-2 The lie-detector pointed at a field the producer was told to leave empty.** C11's
  cross-check scanned the notes for a degraded source, while Procedure 2 had just been changed to
  keep source failures out of the notes — so the corroborating prose could never exist and the
  pair's headline failure mode was detectable only by sampling. FIXED: the producer writes a
  retrieval summary listing every source whose cells are not all `reached`, deliberately
  duplicating the cell statuses, and C11 reconciles the two records against each other.
- **C2-3 Five condition cross-references in the reviewer's provenance file were wrong** — a
  systematic off-by-one from inserting C11 without sweeping. In a package that requires every
  finding to cite a number, that produces findings the producer cannot act on. FIXED, and the
  sweep is now part of the bar-change rule in the conditions file.
- **C2-4 Procedure 1 read corpora with no sanitization requirement.** The record was introduced
  only in Procedure 2, so adversarial content entered the map wave unrecorded. FIXED: sanitization
  is a shared rule across both procedures and C19 applies to both artifact kinds.
- **C2-5 No cell status for "applicable pair, never attempted".** The four statuses covered
  source failure but not the agent choosing to skip a pair, nor the guardrail withholding
  content — so the cheapest compliant recording was `reached, count: 0`. The did-not-look versus
  found-nothing split was still broken, one notch below where cycle 1 fixed it. FIXED:
  `not-attempted` and `content-withheld` statuses, both requiring a cause.

Importants also fixed this round: a schema-validity condition (C21) so a mechanical failure has a
number to cite; the angle brief added to the reviewer's inputs and the applied cap and ordering
signal recorded in the artifact, making the bounding condition judgable; queries recorded as a
list, since a multi-pass cell cannot be reproduced from one query; the spot-check asymmetry
clause (a successful re-probe proves reachable-now-from-here, never that the producer's
`unreachable` was dishonest); the six group types enumerated, which C9's coverage arithmetic
joins on; rolling corpora allowed to record `release: rolling`; candidate-identifier existence
folded into C15; runnable validator invocations with a bounded self-heal; artifact locations
explicitly the caller's business; and the reviewer's disclosure for the present-but-validatorless
state that exists today.

Still open, carried to cycle 3: the producer's no-relevance-cut and notes-discipline promises
have no condition; C2's declared-cap and relation-kind checks are stricter than the producer's
prose; C19's fetched-URL half remains hard to judge without a method-provenance field; the
producer's provenance file is still anonymised where the body now names corpora; and the
subcommand/artifact naming mismatch persists.

## Cycle 3 — 2026-08-03 — fresh reviewer, no prior-cycle memory — VERDICT: findings

Hard rules passed again. Three Criticals, all fixed — and the first of them was introduced by
cycle 2's own fix, which is the pattern worth naming: each round closed the did-not-look versus
found-nothing hole at one level and opened it one level down.

- **C3-1 `not-attempted` was an unbounded, uncorroborated opt-out.** Cycle 2 added the status to
  stop non-attempts being written as zeros. But a producer could mark every cell in an angle
  `not-attempted` with the cause "judged unproductive" and satisfy every condition — the cells
  exist, causes are present, the retrieval summary reconciles perfectly, and the result reads as
  a complete honest coverage record for zero work. The bar already recognised this temptation
  one level up, where a not-run *angle* must have its cause corroborated against the scope;
  the identical temptation at cell level had no such requirement. FIXED: the cause must name the
  specific bound and be consistent with the pairs that were attempted, a blanket repeated cause
  is explicitly not a cause, and a majority-`not-attempted` angle or an all-groups-`not-attempted`
  source is a gap unless the cause is source-specific. Status counts now appear in the retrieval
  summary so the proportion is visible without tallying.

- **C3-2 A not-run angle could not produce a compliant artifact, and the self-heal loop pushed
  toward fabricating one.** The method said a not-run angle records a cause; the coverage
  condition said a cell exists for every applicable pair, with no exemption; and the producer was
  told to self-heal to validator exit 0. Since the validator computes completeness from the map
  and registry, it would emit a FAIL for every missing cell on a legitimately not-run angle, and
  the cheapest repair is to write cells — the cheapest cell being a zero. Four of eight angles
  are conditional, so this is the routine path. The flagship distinction was under the strongest
  mechanical pressure in the whole method, pointing the wrong way. FIXED: a not-run artifact is
  a `not_run` block with no coverage cells at all; the coverage condition carries an explicit
  exemption deferring to the not-run condition; and self-heal must never resolve a FAIL by adding
  a coverage claim that was not gathered.

- **C3-3 The coverage denominator was producer-controlled with no completeness guard.** Coverage
  is computed from the map's group types, and nothing required the six types to be present or
  justified absent — so omitting the attack-pattern type silently emptied one angle, omitting the
  component type emptied another, and the resulting search outputs passed vacuously with the
  novelty phrasing available to narrate the emptiness. The precedent pair guards exactly this and
  the guard was dropped in translation. FIXED in both the method and the first condition: every
  type is present or recorded in the scope guard as an absent type with its reason.

Importants fixed this round: the sanitization condition explicitly loads on a map review too and
its check is split by artifact kind (it was declared as applying to both while sitting only in
the search block, and its text was angle-first so unusable on a map); the registry became a
required input for both kinds; the applicability formula is now stated producer-side rather than
only enforced reviewer-side; the expansion floor moved into the condition, where a recorded cap
of eight and one expansion per group had been passing; queries are checked as a set against the
count; padding gained a home in the boundary condition; `content-withheld` gained the anti-abuse
requirements `unreachable` already had; found-by provenance now names its cell so candidates
reconcile against the cells; and the no-cut rule gained an explicit honest phrasing for an item
kept without an obvious scope link, closing the gap where the only two moves were to invent a
relevance line or to drop the item.

Also: a mobile-client row in the absent-input policy, the rolling-corpus allowance carried into
the versioning condition, the amendments log listed with an explicit not-loaded-at-run-time
note, and the producer description trimmed from 1009 to 920 characters so a wave-2 append does
not breach the cap.

Carried to cycle 4: the duplicate-coverage overlap between the completeness and zeros
conditions; the ordering-signal half of the bounding condition, which is not observable unless
candidates record their ordering value; naming the live-probe conditions in the degradation
clause; the stop-versus-may wording mismatch on a mechanical failure; and the anchor sweep, since
a handful of requirements still live on only one side of the producer/reviewer pair.

## Cycle 4 — 2026-08-03 — fresh reviewer, no prior-cycle memory — VERDICT: findings

Hard rules passed, including a paraphrase check against the precedent pair (six shared n-grams,
all shared idiom; the conditions files share none) and a full numbering audit. Three Criticals:

- **C4-1 Procedure 2 never bound the search to the map's vocabulary.** The map was consumed only
  for group types and the active source list; nothing told the producer to query a group's
  canonical term or expansions, or to apply its negative terms — which Procedure 1 authors and a
  condition grades, but which nothing anywhere consumed. So a cell could be filled with one
  generic query, satisfy completeness, reproducibility and the no-cut arithmetic, and report
  coverage of a group whose terms were never searched. The anti-pattern also named the scope
  context as query authority where it should name the map. FIXED: the map is the sole source of
  query terms, negative terms are applied per cell, and the reproducibility condition now checks
  that a cell's queries come from its own group.
- **C4-2 The mobile angle's precondition contradicted the absent-input policy.** The policy says
  an unstated mobile posture means run the angle and record the assumption; the angle table said
  "ships a mobile client", so silence routed to not-run, and the not-run condition corroborated
  it happily because silence agrees with absence. An entire control family could drop invisibly,
  on the dry-run sample itself. FIXED in both: the precondition includes "or the scope does not
  say", and the condition now treats a not-run cause resting on silence, where the policy directs
  the angle to run, as a gap.
- **C4-3 An empty applicable set was an undeclared third state.** Either factor of the coverage
  product can legitimately compute to zero — every group type of an angle recorded absent, or
  every one of its sources skipped — while the angle's precondition still holds. The output then
  has no cells, the completeness condition passes vacuously over an empty set, and the result
  reads as an honest empty search with nothing recording that the angle was hollowed out
  upstream. FIXED: a `vacated` record naming the empty factor and the map entry responsible, and
  the condition now treats a bare zero-cell output in that situation as a gap.

Importants fixed: the expansion floor gained a relief valve, since a hard floor with no escape
manufactures filler; the cap-drop record now carries ordering values, without which the
dropped-tail check could never fire; found-by became a list so a repeat item is recorded once
with all its cells rather than forcing a choice between broken arithmetic and padding, and the
candidate-to-cell reconciliation became an actual check; the map now records a per-angle
applicability verdict, so an angle judged inapplicable leaves a trace and can be corroborated the
way a not-run angle is; and source stamping keys on the active source list rather than on the
producer's own account of what it "walked", with corpus-specific identifiers in the terms as the
tell that a corpus was read whatever the provenance labels claim.

Also: the misattributed condition number in the reviewer's provenance file corrected, the
both-kinds sanitization condition surfaced in its block header, and the template's
script-validation hard rule restored to the producer's progressive-disclosure section.

## Cycle 5 — 2026-08-03 — fresh reviewer, no prior-cycle memory — VERDICT: findings, ZERO CRITICAL

The forge's last permitted cycle. **No Critical findings.** Hard rules all passed, including a
paraphrase check against the precedent pair and a full numbering audit (C1–C22, no gaps or
duplicates, every cross-reference resolving). The reviewer produced a route map of every way an
agent could fabricate an honest-looking artifact at map, angle, cell and candidate level, and
found the bar closing all but four — those four became the Importants below, and all are fixed:

- **C5-1 A cap drop was recorded angle-wide**, so once the cap fired the per-cell
  returned-versus-kept check became unjudgeable: a reviewer could neither confirm a delta nor
  fault it, and a relevance cut could launder as cap truncation. Each dropped item now names its
  originating cell.
- **C5-2 Nothing checked that a candidate was actually returned by the query its found-by names.**
  Identifiers exist, counts are authorable and found-by is authorable, so internal consistency
  alone could not distinguish an angle worked from an angle written from model knowledge. The
  spot-check condition now samples a candidate against its own query's results, and treats
  absence there as fabrication rather than source drift.
- **C5-3 An absent group type needed a reason but not a corroborated one**, and the condition's
  own calibration blessed the uncorroborated form while its prose called this the
  highest-leverage failure. The parallel negatives elsewhere are corroborated; this one was not.
  Absent types are now corroborated against the scope context, and the empty-set case tells the
  reviewer to re-check the blamed map entry rather than accept the blame-tag.
- **C5-4 No degradation path for a search output handed without its vocabulary map** — the one
  required input that is caller-supplied rather than shipped in the package. Without it the
  validator cannot run and completeness is uncomputable, so the generic "state what you could not
  assess" rule would have permitted approving on almost nothing. Now: say so and stop.

Improvements also fixed: a stamped active source now counts as read and owes a sanitization
record (a map could otherwise stamp six sources from model knowledge and owe none); at least one
broad pass per cell is now required, since an angle of hyper-narrow queries returns honest zeros
having covered nothing and the no-false-revise rule would oblige approval; `returned` named once
as the result count the status table requires; the last portability leak in either package
(a possessive referring to the originating workspace, replaced with one referring to the
collection); and the raw-request rule narrowed to map derivation,
since at search time the gate does enforce it and it was mislabelled as unenforced.

**Disposition: no Critical at the final cycle, so the forge does not abort.** Its exit condition
(zero Critical and zero Important) was not met at cycle 5, which permits shipping with warnings —
but every finding was small and precisely specified, so all were fixed instead. Gate re-run
clean. Note that no sixth cycle is permitted, so these last fixes ship unreviewed by a fresh
reader; they are narrow and additive, and the planted-defect gate is still ahead of them.

